Z||000007||lou_dias||10-15-2001||01:46 AM||||well I guess I suffered a (mild) concusion.<BR>I get dizzy in cars when there is lots of accelerating and decelerating and bumps.  I'll be suing so hopefully I can finally take a vacation this summer.<P>I'll be checking out the car monday and talking to the insurance.<P>It's a black 88 GT 5 speed with 104500 miles and still running strong.  All power option, sunroof, rear window defogger.  Grey interior. No subwoofer though.  I added a 98 Blazer CD player but I'll yank that and throw it back in my 87 if the car is not fixable.<P>I only bought it in May to replace my blown 3.4 87 GT but now that is in the process of a rebuild.  (Good thing nobody decided to buy it off me!)  Not soon enough for me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||lou_dias||10-15-2001||01:52 AM||||the windshield didn't shatter...<BR>I did manage to make HIM leak some fluid though.<P>This is the second truck that's hit a fiero of mine.  My 87 got hit at an angle on the driver's side door by a 96 GMC subeurban and it bounced off and hit a telephone pole and they totalled the suburban.  I fixed the GT, no frame damage.  It was my little brother driving thinking the clutch was the brake.  Not a scratch on him.<P>Yep, these guys with their trucks laugh at the size of Fieros and how they can run them over, but it's my experience that when the two collide, I'd much rather be in the fiero.||||reg||1
